{
  "dom_id": "step-q158357",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Compute $P(X>1)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{27}(3{x}^{2}-{x}^{3}),\\, & 0\\le x\\le 3, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a<X\\le b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)$ is identical to zero for all $x>3,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>1) & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{4}{27}(3{x}^{2}-{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{27}{\\int }_{1}^{3}3{x}^{2}-{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{27}{[{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{27}([(3)^{3}-\\frac{1}{4}(3)^{4}]-[(1)^{3}-\\frac{1}{4}(1)^{4}]) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{27}(27-\\frac{81}{4}-1+\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{27}\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
